  "id": "DrugBank_DB00830 - MONDO_19182",
  "verbalization": "Phenmetrazine is associated with Obesity Disorder, which in turn is linked to several drugs that induce or contribute to Monogenic Obesity. The evidence suggests that Phenmetrazine may act through a shared pathway involving Obesity Disorder, which is a key indicator of genetic susceptibility to obesity. The presence of multiple drugs—Fenfluramine, Orlistat, and Cetilistat—each with distinct mechanisms of action—indicates that the relationship between Phenmetrazine and Monogenic Obesity may be mediated through a common intermediate, Obesity Disorder. This suggests that Phenmetrazine could potentially influence the genetic or metabolic pathways underlying Monogenic Obesity, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Obesity Disorder as a bridge between Phenmetrazine and Monogenic Obesity, emphasizing the role of pharmacological interventions in modulating these pathways.",
